Native Wi-Fi firmware/transport reference notices

Reference: OpenBSD src 65596250e06438442ce07bad87e5ba129229607d,
sys/dev/pci/if_iwx.c (1.230), if_iwxreg.h (1.75), if_iwxvar.h (1.50).
Pyxis selects the permissive BSD alternative for dual-licensed material.
Local changes: bounded native PCI/DMA/interrupt and BSP worker integration;
firmware/NVM/passive scan and bounded legacy open-station/data subset;
native capability ownership and
checked quarantine rather than reference reset/free paths. No LinuxKPI or
OpenBSD kernel compatibility layer. Original integration is MPL-2.0 except retained
reference material under the notices below. Firmware has separate Intel terms.

Additional Linux reference: torvalds/linux tag v6.12,
drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/{pcie/trans.c,iwl-io.c,pcie/ctxt-info.c}.
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause; BSD-3-Clause selected.
Native integration reimplements reset/BISR ordering and bootstrap DMA-span
admission through Pyxis clock/worker/allocator interfaces. No Linux code is
vendored or linked. Source hashes/provenance are in the stage-2 experiment.

